  ],
  "rationale": "The one home (SPEC_STANDARD 15.4) of every policy value Registry's generated code reads that is neither an environment setting (runtime_settings) nor an enumeration member or field type (models): typed constants of the data_provider module (State 3), which a consumer imports by name as the State 5 table 'Constants each module imports' lists (SPEC_STANDARD 6.10, 15.3.1, 15.9). Decided values are carried unchanged from the decisions in source_refs: A13's durations and refusal count, A18's 03:00, look and 30 x 24 hours, A19's 50 MB, A01's 128, A02's 40 (R0-90) and the characteristics' bounds, A17's 32 bytes, A09's rights and highest classes (rows in the enumeration values State 6 declares), A22's one type estimate by PresuPro. Technical values chosen by the author under the owner's delegation of 2026-11-11: the backup prefixes registry-backup- and registry-tmp- (neither begins with the other), the store's temporary suffix .new, STORE_VERSION 1 (the first store of re-authored Registry; the v1 store is not opened, the import reads a file), RELEASE_VERSION registry-2.0.0 and CONTRACT_VERSION registry-contract-2 (v1 being the first). OBJECT_FLOOR_AREA_MIN_EXCLUSIVE is a fixed-precision decimal written as a string (SPEC_STANDARD 15.4). A17's port bounds 1 and 65535 are LISTEN_PORT_MIN and LISTEN_PORT_MAX. Added in State 6 (State 2 round-68 T11 carried the backup key digest here): BACKUP_RECORD_VERSION 1 versions the record line a backup carries readable without its key; BACKUP_KEY_DIGEST_DOMAIN separates the key digest — sha256: and the lowercase hex SHA-256 of the domain's bytes, a zero byte and the key's UTF-8 bytes — from any other use of the key; BACKUP_KEY_DERIVATION_INFO is the HKDF-SHA256 info from which the AES-256-GCM key of a backup is derived. A new algorithm is a new record version, never a reinterpretation of an old one. A04 rule 6's six stages, which every refusal carries as its stage number (State 6 wire format), are six constants REFUSAL_STAGE_AUTHENTICATION 1 to REFUSAL_STAGE_LIFECYCLE 6 (owner, 2026-11-17): Refusal.stage stays an int, and a module names the stage it refuses at by the constant it imports. The first ordinals the design fixes as 1 have one home each (State 7 structure requests, 2026-11-17): REVISION_FIRST, the revision a Project or a Customer is made or imported with (State 1, 'an ordinal starting at 1'), and ACCESS_VERSION_FIRST, an agent session's access version at registration (A12 rule 1). Each later revision or version is one more than the one before; that step is what an ordinal is, not a value of its own. Added 2026-11-17 by the owner's decisions on the State 7 structure requests of operations, service_api and owner_interface: PERSONAL_DATA_FIELDS, the (answer model, field) pairs holding State 1's personal_data facts (A09 rule 4); SERVICE_AGENT_SESSION_HEADER, the header naming Kernel's agent session (R0-53); SERVICE_ANSWER_STATUS and REFUSAL_HTTP_STATUSES, v1's statuses (SOURCE.md L14: not_found 404, internal_error 500, every other code 422); UPLOAD_FORM_HEAD_MAX_BYTES, the bound of the multipart head an upload form sends before its file, its CSRF field first (A13 rule 5), 8192 a technical value delegated to the author. LISTENER_READ_TIMEOUT_SECONDS (30), how long a listener waits for a request's next bytes before closing the connection (State 2 round-90 T8, State 5 round-39 T3), a technical value delegated to the author. Added 2026-11-24 by the owner's decisions on the State 7 structure requests of owner_interface: OWNER_ACTIONS, one row of row model OwnerActionRoute for every OwnerAction member (total, keyed by the action), gives the method and path a request names it by and the two facts its admission needs: is_change, the actions A13 rule 2 calls changes of the session (showing a confirmation step, uploading a file, every submission, a sign-out), whose form carries the CSRF value, and touches_upload, the actions A16 rule 2 lists as reading or changing an uploaded file (an upload, showing the mapping, confirming the import, a sign-out); showing the confirmation step touches the uploaded file only when the action it confirms is the import, which is its confirm_action and not a fact of the action alone. Reads are GET and every other action POST; each path is the action's value after a slash, the project list's the root; no two rows share a method and a path. Sign-in is POST and no change: it carries no session and no CSRF value (A13 rule 4). A request whose method and path name no row names no action, and operations refuses it after stage (1) as a value outside its closed list, as the service API does an operation it does not know. OWNER_TARGET_PARAMETER is the query parameter that carries a request's target, an identity and never a personal value (R0-29); OWNER_CSRF_FIELD the form field, the upload's first multipart part included, that carries the CSRF value; OWNER_SESSION_COOKIE_NAME the session cookie's name, whose __Host- prefix makes a browser keep it only as Secure, for the whole of Registry's origin and for no other host (A13 rule 1; OWASP); it is set SameSite=Strict, so a browser never sends it with a request another site started (owner, 2026-11-24). Owner pages carry SERVICE_ANSWER_STATUS for an answer and the code's row of REFUSAL_HTTP_STATUSES for a refusal, one table for both surfaces. These are technical values chosen by the author under the owner's delegation. Added 2026-11-24 by the owner's decisions on the State 7 structure requests of operations and on the listener prototype of 2026-11-17: OWNER_AUDIT_ACTIONS, rows of row model OwnerAuditAction keyed by the owner action with, for marking a customer, its CustomerTransition and, for erasing a project, its ProjectErasure, gives the AuditAction M09 has an accepted owner action write (R0-58); an action with no row writes no entry. Answering an access request has the grant's row, and operations writes it only when the answer granted a project: a decline changes no session's projects and writes none (M09). LISTENER_CLOSE_DRAIN_SECONDS (2) and LISTENER_CLOSE_DRAIN_MAX_BYTES (64 MiB, more than an upload's IMPORT_FILE_MAX_BYTES with its framing) bound the staged close of a connection answered before its body was read to its end (RFC 9112 section 9.6): the listener shuts its writing side, reads and drops what the client still sends until either bound is reached or the client closes, then closes, so a client still sending receives the answer instead of a reset (prototype listener_proto, 2026-11-17). These are technical values chosen by the author under the owner's delegation.",
